concept :the_face_warrant do
  name "The Face Warrant"
  aka "取面单"
  tags :legibility, :trade, :governance, :water

  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    The written order under which a #{ref :the_preservationists, "Preservationist"} register house spends a face of an admitted piece on behalf of a party outside the settlements. It is executed before the plate touches the piece, and what it settles first is title: the sheet, its album line, the grit and every scraping off the plate stay with the house, and the requesting party receives one certified extract and no property in anything the reading touched.

    The #{ref :juyan_register_house, "Juyan Register House"} has granted fifteen since 2084 and spent eleven faces on them. Twelve of the fifteen came from #{ref :market, "Market"} claim offices working on plant older than the Breach, whose acceptance schedules were migrated between coalition systems rather than rebuilt and are now cited by number in files that hold no text. Two of the remaining three went to a Hong Kong assay house and one to a copying house at Zhangye. The fee is stated in paper and fine grit, both of which come in with the couriers, because #{ref :the_squeeze, "a reading"} spends both and the settlements make neither.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "Before The Plate"
    A request names a subject rather than an admission number because outsiders cannot search the register. The house states whether a piece exists and, when it does, returns its number and remaining face count.

    The requesting party then states the use, and the warrant is written to it. An extract granted on an acceptance question may be filed against that question and nothing else; an office that files one in support of a household line is refused its next request. Title in the sheet and the residue is assigned on the same line, in advance, and the requesting party signs it before the piece leaves its coffer.

    A warrant lapses at the end of the register year in which it was granted. The face goes back into the queue at the position it held and the fee stays with the house. #{ref :entry_into_the_register, "The register"} enters the lapse on the piece's line beside the thickness the reading would have cost.

    An extract's certificate runs thirty-five years from the day it is issued. The entitlement runs against the sheet. A party that wants the figure after that files again, and the second warrant spends a second face.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "What A Warrant Cannot Buy"
    A second sheet off a face that has already given one. No piece leaves the house, and no reader takes a piece outside the class of ware they hold to, so a warrant against a mineral-loaded slab waits for a slab reader and can wait a year.

    No warrant is granted against a piece whose line carries an open contested item. #{ref :the_liangzhou_double_return, "The Liangzhou item"} has stopped four requests, on the reasoning entered with the refusals: an extract carries the house's certificate, and a certificate over a line the settlement cannot close would put a disputed reading into a foreign file where nobody can find the dispute.

    The house also refuses any party whose own records come out of #{ref :the_great_root, "the Great Root"}'s archives, which is why no corridor agency holds an extract. Market's examiners treat the rule as a supplier's preference and pay it without argument. The settlement assembly treats it as the whole of what holding a register in trust consists of, and has entered that reasoning with each refusal.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :trade, heading: "The Carriage"
    Requests and counterfoils move on the western run with #{ref :the_brokers, "the Pearl River houses"}, who take the paper as ordinary freight and charge for it as such. #{ref :yao_lin, "Yao Lin"} has carried five warrants inbound and four counterfoils out.

    The extract travels as two sheets: the certified copy, and the counterfoil the house keeps a duplicate of, carrying the admission number, the face number, the album line and the date the thirty-five years begin. #{ref :race_street_warehouse, "The Race Street warehouse"} keeps both behind Ruth Osei's table.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — Title in the sheet and the residue is assigned in writing before the lapping, from museum destructive-sampling agreements: anything remaining after a destructive analysis, and every new preparation made from it, stays the property of the repository unless a curator agreed otherwise before the sample was taken. The irreversibility had to be priced before the act, so the warrant is an assignment executed while the piece is still in its coffer."
  log "2026-08-09 — The two intervals come from unclaimed-property custody, where tangible property may be converted to a fungible substitute after a short dormancy while the owner's claim survives against the substitute for a much longer term. That gave the warrant a short lapse — one register year, after which the face returns to the queue — and a long one over which the extract rather than the piece carries the entitlement."
end
